title: The first red autumn

@assessment
title: July 2023 assessment
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
on-arrival: {!
Q.prototype_complete = 1;
Q.left_poll = Math.round(Q.left_poll * 10) / 10;
Q.ending_score = 0;
Q.ending_2021_events = [
    Q.vaccine_event_done,
    Q.rename_event_done,
    Q.recovery_fund_event_done,
    Q.opposition_reset_event_done,
    Q.left_revolt_event_done
].reduce(function(total, completed) {
    return total + (completed ? 1 : 0);
}, 0);
Q.ending_score += Q.ending_2021_events;
Q.ending_extension_events = [
    Q.august_2021_done,
    Q.border_2021_done,
    Q.october_2021_done,
    Q.november_2021_done,
    Q.december_2021_done,
    Q.polish_deal_2022_done,
    Q.ukraine_invasion_done,
    Q.ukraine_refugees_done,
    Q.war_economy_2022_done,
    Q.rates_lists_2022_done,
    Q.kpo_2022_done,
    Q.inflation_2022_done,
    Q.odra_2022_done,
    Q.energy_2022_done,
    Q.konf_succession_2022_done,
    Q.november_2022_done,
    Q.budget_2022_done,
    Q.kpo_bill_2023_done,
    Q.february_2023_done,
    Q.church_2023_done,
    Q.third_way_2023_done,
    Q.lex_tusk_2023_done,
    Q.june_2023_done,
    Q.july_2023_done
].reduce(function(total, completed) {
    return total + (completed ? 1 : 0);
}, 0);
Q.ending_score += Math.floor(Q.ending_extension_events / 4);
if (Q.party_unity >= 50) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.party_unity >= 65) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.left_vote_intent >= 10) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.left_vote_intent >= 13) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.labor_credibility >= 50) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.progressive_credibility >= 55) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.feminist_trust >= 50) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.media_capacity + Q.local_network >= 70) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.budget_2019_ratified) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.budget_2020_ratified) Q.ending_score += 2;
if (Q.presidential_result >= 5) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.trz_inaugurated) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.public_trust >= 50) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.judicial_legitimacy + Q.constitutional_restraint >= 100) {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (Q.health_capacity + Q.household_security >= 110) {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (Q.psl_relation >= 35 || Q.president_relation >= 35) {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (
    Q.movement_autonomy >= 65 &&
    Q.organiser_energy >= 55
) {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (Q.vaccination_strategy == "Public-health mobilisation" ||
    Q.vaccination_strategy == "Local access") {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (Q.recovery_fund_strategy != "Abstention") Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.budget_2021_ratified) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.budget_2022_ratified) Q.ending_score += 2;
if (Q.opposition_reset_strategy) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.merger_resolution == "Five-current truce" ||
    Q.merger_resolution == "Razem-led current pact" ||
    Q.merger_resolution == "Membership ballot") {
    Q.ending_score += 1;
}
if (Q.leadership_actions_taken >= 38) Q.ending_score += 1;
if (Q.leadership_actions_taken >= 43) Q.ending_score += 1;

if (Q.trz_oath_crisis_launched && Q.trz_repeat_winner == "Andrzej Duda") {
    Q.ending_presidential_route =
        "Trzaskowski won the count; Witek's interregnum and a disputed court invalidity forced a repeat election";
} else if (Q.trz_inaugurated) {
    Q.ending_presidential_route =
        "Trzaskowski was sworn in; cohabitation pressure " +
        Math.round(Number(Q.trz_cohabitation_temperature) || 0) +
        ", right backlash " +
        Math.round(Number(Q.trz_right_backlash) || 0);
} else {
    Q.ending_presidential_route =
        Q.pres_runoff_winner_name + " won the presidency";
}

if (
    Q.ending_score >= 31 &&
    Q.party_unity >= 60 &&
    Q.budget_2019_ratified &&
    Q.budget_2020_ratified
) {
    Q.ending_name = "Polish Red Autumn";
} else if (
    Q.ending_score >= 26 &&
    Q.party_unity >= 45 &&
    Q.budget_2020_ratified
) {
    Q.ending_name = "A rebuilt Left";
} else if (Q.ending_score >= 20 && Q.party_unity >= 25) {
    Q.ending_name = "Relevant opposition";
} else {
    Q.ending_name = "Survival";
}
!}

= [+ ending_name +]

The campaign chapter ends in **July 2023**.

Lewica modelled vote: **[+ left_vote_intent +]%**  
Alliance unity: **[+ party_unity +]/100**  
Presidential result: **[+ presidential_result +]%**  
Presidential route: **[+ ending_presidential_route +]**  
2020 budget backing: **[+ budget_backing +]%**  
Media plus local capacity: **[+ media_capacity +] + [+ local_network +]**
Merger resolution: **[+ merger_resolution +]**  
2021 sequence completed: **[+ ending_2021_events +] / 5**  
2021–2023 extension completed: **[+ ending_extension_events +] / 24**  
Leadership months used: **[+ leadership_actions_taken +] / 45**  
Neglected months: **[+ neglected_months +]**

[? if ending_name = "Polish Red Autumn": The alliance has done more than
survive. It now has a programme, a cadre base, movement links not owned by any
single faction, and enough public weight to challenge for leadership of the
opposition. The harder chapter - merger, KPO, government, and the eventual
Razem split - now begins from a position of strength. ?]

[? if ending_name = "A rebuilt Left": The component parties still distrust one
another, but they now have reasons to remain in the same room. The Left enters
2021 with recognisable assets, a social base that can still be mobilised, and
more than borrowed parliamentary relevance. ?]

[? if ending_name = "Relevant opposition": The alliance remains useful and
visible. It still has not answered the strategic question at its core: is this
a party, a list, or only a truce between factions with different futures? ?]

[? if ending_name = "Survival": No component has found a safer exit, which is
not the same as unity. The Left survives the year and carries every unresolved
argument, debt and grievance forward into the merger period. ?]

[? if trz_oath_crisis_launched and trz_repeat_winner = "Andrzej Duda": The certified presidential result never became an oath.
PiS proved that institutional command could override an election result; every
later opposition strategy now begins with that institutional defeat. ?]

[? if trz_oath_crisis_launched and trz_inaugurated: Witek's acting claim did
not survive the imposed rerun, but the constitutional and foreign-policy damage
did. Trzaskowski enters the Palace only after winning the presidency twice.?]

[? if trz_inaugurated: The Palace survived the certification fight and became
a hostile centre of power inside the PiS government. Its vetoes split the United
Right, while the same conflict gave PiS and Konfederacja a durable campaign
against obstruction and liberal Warsaw. ?]

[? if trz_inaugurated and trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Passed and signed":
**[+ trz_rights_bill +]** reached the Palace and became law. Trzaskowski kept
the no-veto pledge; the right carries the reversal campaign into the next
chapter. ?]

[? if trz_inaugurated and trz_rights_bill_outcome = "Defeated in the Sejm":
The Palace promised a signature on **[+ trz_rights_bill +]**, but the bill
never escaped the PiS Sejm. A friendly pen did not create a majority. ?]

- @restart: Return to the title
- @library: Review the Polish dossier

@prepare_epilogue
title: Prepare the Polish epilogue
on-arrival: {!
const endingNumber = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};
const endingClamp = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, value));
};
const snapResultAvailable = Q.snap_election_complete && Q.snap_election_held;
const votedOut = Q.ending_exit_type == "Voted out" ||
    ((Q.election_2023_seen || snapResultAvailable) &&
        endingNumber(Q.left_seats, 0) == 0);
const lostByThreshold = votedOut && (snapResultAvailable
    ? endingNumber(Q.snap_election_left_vote, 0) < 5
    : endingNumber(Q.election_2023_filed_committee_seats, 0) == 0);
Q.prototype_complete = 1;
Q.poland_event_phase = 0;
Q.poland_legacy_event_phase = 0;
Q.timeline_complete = votedOut ? 0 : 1;
Q.ending_exit_type = votedOut ? "Voted out" : "Natural conclusion";
Q.ending_exit_date = Q.date_label ||
    ((Q.month_name || "December") + " " + (Q.year || 2026));
const endingElectionYear = Math.round(endingNumber(Q.year, 2023));
const endingYearsSince2015 = Math.max(1, endingElectionYear - 2015);
Q.ending_campaign_years = Math.max(1, endingElectionYear - 2019);
const endingNextOrganisationalTest = endingElectionYear <= 2023
    ? "the 2024 local and European campaigns"
    : "the next local and European campaigns";
Q.left_poll = Math.round(endingNumber(Q.left_poll, 0) * 10) / 10;
Q.ending_budget_wins = [
    Q.annual_budget_done_2023 && Q.annual_budget_passed_2023,
    Q.annual_budget_done_2024 && Q.annual_budget_passed_2024,
    Q.annual_budget_done_2025 && Q.annual_budget_passed_2025,
    Q.annual_budget_done_2026 && Q.annual_budget_passed_2026
].reduce(function(total, result) {
    return total + (result ? 1 : 0);
}, 0);
Q.ending_judiciary_score = Math.round(
    (
        endingNumber(Q.tribunal_composition_legality, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.tribunal_domestic_recognition, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.krs_independence, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.supreme_court_chamber_recognition, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.prosecution_command_clarity, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.european_judgment_compliance, 40) +
        endingNumber(Q.court_user_trust, 40) +
        (100 - endingNumber(Q.legal_dualism, 60)) +
        (100 - endingNumber(Q.court_backlog, 60))
    ) / 9
);
const endingLeftOrganisations = [
    ["left", 1, Q.left_party_name || "Lewica", "left_seats"],
    [
        "sld_breakaway", Q.barons_party_formed,
        Q.barons_party_name || "Democratic Left Alliance",
        "sld_breakaway_seats"
    ],
    [
        "social_patriot", Q.social_patriot_party_formed,
        Q.social_patriot_party_name || "Lewica Patriotyczna",
        "social_patriot_seats"
    ],
    [
        "spring_breakaway", Q.spring_party_formed,
        Q.spring_party_name || "Spring", "spring_breakaway_seats"
    ],
    [
        "labor_left", Q.labor_party_formed,
        Q.labor_party_name || "Labour Left", "labor_left_seats"
    ],
    [
        "young_left", Q.progressives_party_formed,
        Q.progressives_party_name || "Young Left", "young_left_seats"
    ],
    ["razem", Q.razem_party_formed, Q.razem_party_name || "Razem", "razem_party_seats"],
    ["pps", Q.pps_party_formed, Q.pps_party_name || "PPS", "pps_party_seats"]
].filter(function(entry) {
    return entry[1];
});
const endingMainCommittee = {
    left_coalition_8: "left_coalition",
    razem_5: "razem",
    democratic_8: "democratic_list",
    ko_5: "ko",
    third_way_8: "third_way",
    third_host_5: String(Q.sejm_list_host || "psl"),
    pis_5: "pis"
}[String(Q.sejm_list_outcome || "left_5")] || "left";
const endingCommitteeFor = {
    left: endingMainCommittee,
    sld_breakaway: "sld_breakaway",
    social_patriot: String(
        Q.social_patriot_list_committee || "social_patriot"
    ),
    spring_breakaway: String(
        Q.spring_list_committee || "spring_breakaway"
    ),
    labor_left: String(Q.labor_list_committee || "labor_left"),
    young_left: String(Q.progressives_list_committee || "young_left"),
    razem: String(Q.razem_list_committee || "razem"),
    pps: "pps"
};
const endingCommitteeThreshold = {
    left_coalition: 8,
    democratic_list: 8,
    third_way: 8
};
const endingVote = function(id) {
    return endingNumber(
        Q[(snapResultAvailable ? "snap_election_" : "election_2023_") +
            id + "_vote"],
        endingNumber(Q[id + "_vote_intent"], 0)
    );
};
const endingCommitteeVote = function(id) {
    if (snapResultAvailable) return endingVote(id);
    return endingNumber(
        Q["election_2023_" + id + "_committee_vote"],
        endingVote(id)
    );
};
const endingLeftCommittees = [];
for (const organisation of endingLeftOrganisations) {
    const committee = snapResultAvailable
        ? organisation[0]
        : (endingCommitteeFor[organisation[0]] || organisation[0]);
    if (!endingLeftCommittees.includes(committee)) {
        endingLeftCommittees.push(committee);
    }
}
Q.ending_electoral_organisations = endingLeftOrganisations.length;
Q.ending_fragmentation_lists = endingLeftCommittees.length;
Q.ending_lists_above_threshold = endingLeftCommittees.reduce(
    function(total, entry) {
        return total + (
            endingCommitteeVote(entry) >=
                (endingCommitteeThreshold[entry] || 5)
                ? 1 : 0
        );
    },
    0
);
Q.ending_threshold_losses = endingLeftCommittees.reduce(
    function(total, entry) {
        return total + (
            endingCommitteeVote(entry) <
                (endingCommitteeThreshold[entry] || 5)
                ? 1 : 0
        );
    },
    0
);
Q.ending_family_vote = Math.round(
    endingLeftOrganisations.reduce(function(total, entry) {
        return total + Math.max(0, endingVote(entry[0]));
    }, 0) * 10
) / 10;
const actualLeftFamilySeats = [
    "left_seats", "sld_breakaway_seats", "social_patriot_seats",
    "spring_breakaway_seats",
    "labor_left_seats", "young_left_seats", "razem_party_seats",
    "pps_party_seats"
].reduce(function(total, quality) {
    return total + Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q[quality], 0));
}, 0);
Q.ending_family_seats = Math.max(0, Math.round(votedOut || snapResultAvailable
    ? actualLeftFamilySeats
    : endingNumber(Q.left_family_projected_seats, actualLeftFamilySeats)));
const endingCleanName = function(value) {
    return String(value || "Lewica")
        .replace(/Lewica Lewic/g, "Porozumienie Lewicy")
        .replace(/\s+/g, " ")
        .trim();
};
const endingSeries = function(items) {
    if (!items.length) return "";
    if (items.length == 1) return items[0];
    if (items.length == 2) return items[0] + " and " + items[1];
    return items.slice(0, -1).join(", ") + ", and " + items[items.length - 1];
};
const endingVoteText = function(value) {
    return (Math.round(value * 100) / 100).toFixed(2)
        .replace(/0+$/, "").replace(/\.$/, "");
};
Q.ending_player_party_name = endingCleanName(Q.left_party_name);
const endingOrganisationResults = endingLeftOrganisations.map(
    function(entry) {
        const seats = Math.max(0, Math.round(endingNumber(Q[entry[3]], 0)));
        return endingCleanName(entry[2]) + " " +
            endingVoteText(endingVote(entry[0])) + "% (" + seats +
            " seat" + (seats == 1 ? "" : "s") + ")";
    }
);
Q.ending_left_organisations = endingSeries(endingOrganisationResults);
Q.ending_left_names = endingSeries(endingLeftOrganisations.map(
    function(entry) { return endingCleanName(entry[2]); }
));
Q.ending_2015_comparison = lostByThreshold
    ? (actualLeftFamilySeats > 0
        ? (
            "In 2015, Zjednoczona Lewica won 7.55% and missed the 8% " +
            "coalition threshold, leaving the post-1989 Sejm without a " +
            "parliamentary left for the first time. " +
            endingYearsSince2015 + " years later your " +
            "committee suffers the same legal defeat, while rival Left " +
            "organisations return with " + actualLeftFamilySeats +
            " seats. The tradition survives in parliament; your claim to " +
            "lead it does not."
        )
        : (
        "In 2015, Zjednoczona Lewica won 7.55% and missed the 8% " +
        "coalition threshold, producing the first post-1989 Sejm without " +
        "a parliamentary left. " + endingYearsSince2015 +
        " years later the shock has returned, " +
        "but the excuse is weaker: 2015 was one coalition defeated by one " +
        "threshold; this campaign ends with " +
        Q.ending_electoral_organisations + " rival Left organisations and " +
        Q.ending_fragmentation_lists + " filed committees unable to elect " +
        "a single deputy."
        ))
    : (
        "The comparison is 2015, when Zjednoczona Lewica's 7.55% failed " +
        "against an 8% coalition threshold and the Left vanished from the " +
        "Sejm. This defeat is stranger. The filed committee crossed its " +
        "threshold, but its candidate allocation returned no deputy from " +
        "the organisation you controlled."
    );

const endingThirdWayText = Q.third_way_split
    ? "Polska 2050 " + Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q.p2050_seats, 0)) +
        " and PSL " + Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q.psl_seats, 0))
    : "Third Way " + Math.max(
        0,
        endingNumber(Q.p2050_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.psl_seats, 0)
    );
Q.ending_chamber_result =
    "The certified chamber gives PiS " +
    Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q.pis_seats, 0)) + " seats, KO " +
    Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q.ko_seats, 0)) + ", " +
    endingThirdWayText + ", and Konfederacja " +
    Math.max(0, endingNumber(Q.konf_seats, 0)) + ". The whole Left family " +
    "holds " + actualLeftFamilySeats + " seats. Any investiture majority can " +
    "therefore be assembled without the organisation your leadership spent " +
    Q.ending_campaign_years + " years trying to consolidate.";

const endingMajority = Math.max(
    1,
    Math.round(endingNumber(Q.sejm_statutory_majority, 231))
);
const endingCentreSeats =
    endingNumber(Q.ko_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.p2050_seats, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.psl_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.centrum_seats, 0);
const endingBroadDemocraticSeats = endingCentreSeats + actualLeftFamilySeats;
const endingRightSeats =
    endingNumber(Q.pis_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.konf_seats, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.rozwoj_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.korona_seats, 0);
const endingPisPslSeats =
    endingNumber(Q.pis_seats, 0) + endingNumber(Q.psl_seats, 0);
const endingPresident = Q.president_name || "the President";
if (endingNumber(Q.pis_seats, 0) >= endingMajority) {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "PiS holds a majority of its own. " + endingPresident +
        " can renew a Morawiecki cabinet without a single Left vote, and " +
        "Kaczynski can close the chapter on coalition pluralism as a finished experiment.";
} else if (endingCentreSeats >= endingMajority) {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "KO, Poland 2050, PSL and the democratic centre hold " +
        endingCentreSeats + " seats between them. The arithmetic points to a " +
        (Q.ko_leader || "Donald Tusk") +
        "-led cabinet that needs no red vote and can appropriate popular " +
        "pieces of the Left programme without granting its authors office.";
} else if (
    endingBroadDemocraticSeats >= endingMajority && actualLeftFamilySeats > 0
) {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "The democratic centre is short on its own but reaches " +
        endingBroadDemocraticSeats + " with the rival Left deputies who did " +
        "survive. Formation passes through their clubs, not yours.";
} else if (
    endingPisPslSeats >= endingMajority &&
    (
        endingRightSeats < endingMajority ||
        endingNumber(Q.coalition_pis_psl_score, 36) >=
            endingNumber(Q.coalition_right_score, 28)
    )
) {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "PiS and PSL can command " + endingPisPslSeats + " seats. The next " +
        "government depends on Kosiniak-Kamysz deciding whether replacing " +
        "the vanished Left as PiS's social partner is rescue or surrender.";
} else if (endingRightSeats >= endingMajority) {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "PiS, Konfederacja and the surviving right-wing splinters hold " +
        endingRightSeats + " seats. A right cabinet can take office without " +
        "a single negotiation across the old opposition aisle.";
} else {
    Q.ending_next_government =
        "No bloc reaches " + endingMajority + ". " + endingPresident +
        " must begin formation in a hung Sejm where PSL and individual " +
        "defectors matter more than the entire extra-parliamentary Left. A " +
        "minority cabinet or another election is now likelier than a " +
        "government built around your programme.";
}

const endingWasInGovernment = Boolean(
    Q.pre_election_left_in_government || Q.left_in_government
);
const endingOutgoingParty = String(
    Q.pre_election_government_party || Q.government_party || ""
);
const endingOutgoingName = String(
    Q.pre_election_government_name || Q.government_name || "the outgoing cabinet"
);
if (votedOut && endingWasInGovernment) {
    Q.ending_outgoing_cabinet = endingOutgoingParty == "pis"
        ? (
            "The verdict also ends the New Left experiment inside " +
            endingOutgoingName + ". Social ministries left policies that can " +
            "still be defended, but the junior partner is erased while PiS " +
            "remains in command of parliamentary arithmetic. That is not " +
            "ordinary coalition blur. It is electoral annexation."
        )
        : (
            "The outgoing cabinet loses its Left delegation on election " +
            "night. Ministers may leave files and enacted measures behind; " +
            "without deputies, they cannot supply confidence to any successor."
        );
} else {
    Q.ending_outgoing_cabinet =
        "The outgoing cabinet will bargain over its successor. The Left now " +
        "watches those talks from party offices, municipalities and studio " +
        "tables rather than from the chamber floor.";
}
Q.ending_fragmentation_penalty =
    Math.max(0, Q.ending_fragmentation_lists - 1) * 2 +
    Q.ending_threshold_losses * 2;
Q.ending_major_reform_score =
    endingNumber(Q.abortion_reform_stage, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.marriage_reform_stage, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.labor_reform_stage, 0);
Q.ending_score =
    Math.round(endingNumber(Q.party_unity, 0) / 10) +
    Math.round(endingNumber(Q.ending_family_vote, 0) / 2) +
    Math.round(endingNumber(Q.public_trust, 0) / 12) +
    Math.round(
        (endingNumber(Q.media_capacity, 0) +
            endingNumber(Q.local_network, 0)) / 20
    ) +
    Q.ending_budget_wins * 3 +
    Math.round(Q.ending_judiciary_score / 12) +
    Math.round(Q.ending_major_reform_score / 2) +
    (Q.left_in_government ? 4 : 0) +
    (Q.pres_2025_round_one_done &&
        Q.pres_2025_winner == Q.pres_2025_left_candidate ? 6 : 0) -
    Q.ending_fragmentation_penalty - (votedOut ? 8 : 0);
if (votedOut) {
    Q.ending_name = actualLeftFamilySeats > 0
        ? "The centre is voted out"
        : (Q.ending_family_vote >= 5
            ? "Votes without representation"
            : "The red benches empty");
} else if (
    Q.party_unity >= 65 &&
    Q.ending_family_vote >= 13 &&
    Q.ending_threshold_losses == 0 &&
    Q.ending_budget_wins >= 3 &&
    Q.ending_judiciary_score >= 55 &&
    (Q.left_in_government || (Q.coalition_status || "").indexOf("Left") >= 0)
) {
    Q.ending_name = "The impossible majority";
} else if (
    Q.ending_family_vote >= 9 &&
    Q.ending_lists_above_threshold >= 1 &&
    Q.ending_budget_wins >= 2
) {
    Q.ending_name = "A Left that can govern";
} else if (
    Q.ending_family_vote >= 5 &&
    Q.ending_lists_above_threshold >= 1
) {
    Q.ending_name = "Survival with leverage";
} else {
    Q.ending_name = "The long fragmentation";
}
Q.ending_constitutional_status = votedOut
    ? "The electorate removed the player-controlled list from the Sejm"
    : (Q.snap_campaign_active
        ? "Parliament dissolved; snap-election polling day falls after the playable horizon"
        : (Q.snap_repeated_deadlock
            ? "Two elections ended without an investiture majority"
            : "No unresolved election campaign at the horizon"));

const publicLegacy = (
    endingNumber(Q.public_trust, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.issue_ownership, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.winner_reputation, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.electoral_viability, 0)
) / 4 - endingNumber(Q.coalition_blur, 0) * 0.12;
if (publicLegacy >= 62) {
    Q.ending_public_memory =
    "Public memory retains a Left that made its quarrels look like arguments about governing Poland, not merely surviving inside coalition machinery.";
} else if (publicLegacy >= 48) {
    Q.ending_public_memory =
        "The public record is mixed but durable: voters can still name what the Left defended, even when they reject parts of the bargaining and personalities.";
} else if (publicLegacy >= 34) {
    Q.ending_public_memory =
        "Achievements remain visible, but so does the blur. Many voters remember the Left as a pressure group inside another party's governing story.";
} else {
    Q.ending_public_memory =
        "By the end, public memory reduces the project to quarrels, tactical votes and promises that never hardened into a convincing claim to power.";
}

if (votedOut) {
    Q.ending_party_future =
        "The authority of " +
        (Q.left_leader || "the last national leadership") +
        " now ends at " + Q.ending_player_party_name + "'s door. " +
        Q.ending_left_names +
        " retain their own executives, debts, mailing lists and accounts of " +
        "who caused the defeat. Parliamentary offices close immediately; " +
        "municipal councillors, union organisers and the remaining staff must " +
        "decide which of those organisations is still worth carrying.";
} else if (
    Q.ending_electoral_organisations >= 4 || Q.ending_threshold_losses >= 2
) {
    Q.ending_party_future =
        "The common Left is now a family of rival organisations. " +
        (Q.left_leader || "the remaining leadership") +
        " controls one inheritance, not the whole tradition; the next congresses will negotiate reunification, dominance, or permanent separation.";
} else if (Q.ending_electoral_organisations >= 2) {
    Q.ending_party_future =
        "The old umbrella has become a negotiated party system. " +
        (Q.left_leader || "the party leadership") +
        " can still assemble common lists, but no faction will again confuse cooperation with self-erasure.";
} else if (Q.party_unity >= 65) {
    Q.ending_party_future =
        "The merger finally resembles a party rather than a ceasefire. Under " +
        (Q.left_leader || "its elected leadership") +
        ", disputes pass through rules strong enough to survive the next succession.";
} else {
    Q.ending_party_future =
        "One legal party survives, but its currents retain separate memories, patrons and exit plans. " +
        (Q.left_leadership_result || "The leadership settlement") +
        " postpones the next structural argument rather than resolving it.";
}

const achievements = [];
const leftPresidentialWin = Q.pres_2025_round_one_done &&
    Q.pres_2025_winner == Q.pres_2025_left_candidate;
if (leftPresidentialWin) {
    achievements.push("a Left candidate captured the Presidency in 2025");
}
if (Q.ending_budget_wins >= 3) {
    achievements.push(Q.ending_budget_wins +
        " post-transfer budgets survived the Sejm");
}
if (Q.ending_judiciary_score >= 60) {
    achievements.push("the judicial settlement left the courts more coherent and legitimate");
}
if (endingNumber(Q.abortion_reform_stage, 0) >= 1) {
    achievements.push(
        "reproductive-rights reform closed with " +
        Q.abortion_reform_stage_label
    );
}
if (endingNumber(Q.marriage_reform_stage, 0) >= 1) {
    achievements.push(
        "legal recognition reached " + Q.marriage_reform_stage_label
    );
}
if (endingNumber(Q.labor_reform_stage, 0) >= 1) {
    achievements.push(
        "labour reconstruction closed with " + Q.labor_reform_stage_label
    );
} else if (endingNumber(Q.labor_credibility, 0) >= 60) {
    achievements.push(
        "labour credibility survived without a national reform settlement"
    );
}
if (endingNumber(Q.media_capacity, 0) + endingNumber(Q.local_network, 0) >= 110) {
    achievements.push("a durable local and media organisation outlived the campaign cycle");
}
if (!achievements.length) {
    achievements.push("the Left remained an organised national tradition through years that could have dissolved it");
}
Q.ending_achievements = achievements.join("; ") + ".";
Q.ending_signature_achievement = achievements[0] + ".";

const failures = [];
if (votedOut) {
    failures.push(lostByThreshold
        ? Q.ending_player_party_name +
            " failed to carry its filed committee across the Sejm threshold"
        : "the host committee entered the Sejm without electing one of your deputies");
}
if (Q.ending_threshold_losses > 0) {
    failures.push(Q.ending_threshold_losses +
        " Left list" + (Q.ending_threshold_losses == 1 ? "" : "s") +
        " converted votes into no representation");
}
if (!votedOut && Q.ending_budget_wins < 2) {
    failures.push("too few annual budgets produced a stable record of delivery");
}
if (Q.ending_judiciary_score < 45) {
    failures.push("the court settlement carried legal dualism into the next decade");
}
if (endingNumber(Q.public_trust, 0) < 40) {
    failures.push("public trust finished below the level needed for a persuasive governing claim");
}
if (endingNumber(Q.coalition_blur, 0) >= 60) {
    failures.push("coalition responsibility obscured which changes belonged to the Left");
}
if (endingNumber(Q.organised_left_splits, 0) >= 2) {
    failures.push("repeated organised splits turned internal pluralism into electoral competition");
}
if (Number(Q.pres_2025_oath_crisis) == 3) {
    failures.push(
        "the Hołownia oath delay collapsed only after a constitutional and foreign-policy crisis"
    );
}
if (!failures.length) {
    failures.push("success never resolved the tension between movement autonomy, party discipline and coalition office");
}
Q.ending_failures = failures.join("; ") + ".";

const organisation = (
    endingNumber(Q.media_capacity, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.local_network, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.organiser_energy, 0)
) / 3;
Q.ending_future_strength = endingClamp(
    Q.ending_family_vote * 2.1 +
    endingNumber(Q.electoral_viability, 0) * 0.18 +
    endingNumber(Q.public_trust, 0) * 0.12 +
    endingNumber(Q.party_unity, 0) * 0.12 +
    organisation * 0.18 -
    Q.ending_fragmentation_penalty * 1.4 -
    (votedOut ? 14 : 0),
    0,
    100
);
if (Q.ending_future_strength >= 66) {
    Q.ending_future_path =
        "By the early 2030s, the Left is again one of the poles around which governments are built. Its younger ministers and organisers inherit institutions, not only a famous defeat, and every coalition negotiation must account for the possibility that it could lead the cabinet itself.";
} else if (Q.ending_future_strength >= 50) {
    Q.ending_future_path =
        "Through the early 2030s, the Left remains a necessary coalition force: rarely dominant, never safely ignored. Its future depends on converting visible municipal, labour and parliamentary work into an electorate that no longer deserts it for the largest anti-right list.";
} else if (Q.ending_future_strength >= 32) {
    Q.ending_future_path =
        "The election cycles around 2030 force a painful consolidation. Some names and logos disappear, but local networks, unions and rights campaigns still provide material for a return, smaller than the old alliance and clearer about why it exists.";
} else {
    Q.ending_future_path =
        "By the early 2030s, the parliamentary Left is absent or peripheral. Its inheritance survives in municipalities, unions and movements until another generation rebuilds under another name; whether that is recovery or replacement remains contested.";
}
if (votedOut) {
    if (Q.ending_future_strength >= 50) {
        Q.ending_future_path =
            "The first chance to reverse the verdict comes before another " +
            "Sejm election: " + endingNextOrganisationalTest + ". A common " +
            "committee could turn surviving mayors, councillors, union halls " +
            "and movement networks into the beginnings of a return. Failure " +
            "to agree one would instead teach a generation of voters to look " +
            "for social policy inside KO or PiS. By 2030, recovery is possible, " +
            "but only through a refoundation in which several current names " +
            "and leadership claims disappear.";
    } else if (Q.ending_future_strength >= 32) {
        Q.ending_future_path =
            endingNextOrganisationalTest.charAt(0).toUpperCase() +
            endingNextOrganisationalTest.slice(1) +
            " become survival tests rather " +
            "than rehearsals for government. One part of the old Left is " +
            "likely to retreat into municipal and trade-union work, another " +
            "to seek places on KO lists, and another to preserve ideological " +
            "independence below the threshold. A parliamentary return around " +
            "2030 remains possible, but it will look more like a new party " +
            "built from the ruins than a reunion of equal heirs.";
    } else {
        Q.ending_future_path =
            "The immediate future is contraction: lost parliamentary offices, " +
            "departing staff, rival congresses and local organisations deciding " +
            "whether the national label still helps them. " +
            endingNextOrganisationalTest.charAt(0).toUpperCase() +
            endingNextOrganisationalTest.slice(1) +
            " scatter the survivors further. By 2030, labour, " +
            "housing and equality politics remain alive, but the party family " +
            "that once claimed them has become historical material for somebody " +
            "else's refoundation.";
    }
}

const democraticLegacy = (
    Q.ending_judiciary_score +
    endingNumber(Q.institutional_trust, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.constitutional_restraint, 0) +
    endingNumber(Q.minority_safety, 0) -
    endingNumber(Q.far_right_agenda, 0) * 0.5
) / 3.5;
Q.ending_national_future = democraticLegacy >= 60
    ? "Poland enters the next decade with democratic conflict still fierce, but with courts, civic organisations and constitutional habits strong enough to survive another transfer of power."
    : (democraticLegacy >= 42
        ? "Poland enters the next decade without settled constitutional peace. Every later government inherits both repaired institutions and precedents for bypassing them."
        : "The unresolved constitutional war becomes the inheritance of the 2030s. Governments change, but distrust, legal dualism and a stronger radical right make each transfer of power feel provisional.");

if (votedOut) {
    Q.ending_vote_out_cause = lostByThreshold
        ? "The filed committee did not clear its legal threshold."
        : "The filed committee won seats, but its candidate allocation elected none of your deputies.";
    Q.ending_opening =
        Q.ending_exit_date + ". At headquarters the national map finishes " +
        "changing colour, the last district protocols are entered, and the " +
        "number beside " + Q.ending_player_party_name + " remains zero. No " +
        "candidate will take the oath. No whip will count a doubtful deputy. " +
        "The next Sejm will conduct every argument in which you once held " +
        "leverage without you.";
    Q.ending_coda = actualLeftFamilySeats > 0
        ? "The red benches are not empty. They now belong to deputies who no longer answer your calls."
        : "In 2015 the Left could say that one threshold had defeated one coalition. In " +
            endingElectionYear +
            ", every red banner arrives at the same locked door.";
    Q.news_headline = Q.ending_player_party_name +
        " is eliminated from the Sejm";
} else {
    Q.ending_opening = Q.election_2027_terminal
        ? Q.ending_exit_date + ". The Sejm and Senate counts are certified. " +
            "The playable campaign ends where its accumulated alliances, " +
            "splits and governing record finally meet the electorate."
        : (Q.snap_campaign_active
        ? Q.ending_exit_date + ". The playable horizon closes while a " +
            "constitutionally scheduled campaign is still underway. There " +
            "is no invented polling-day result—only the country and " +
            "organisation you carry into it."
        : Q.ending_exit_date + ". The constitutional horizon closes without " +
            "inventing an election after an earlier dissolution reset the " +
            "parliamentary term.");
    Q.ending_coda = Q.ending_future_strength >= 50
        ? "You do not leave behind a finished Left. You leave behind one with a future large enough to fight over."
        : "History does not preserve the plan exactly as written. It preserves the institutions, grudges and people still capable of trying again.";
    Q.news_headline = Q.election_2027_terminal
        ? "The 2027 parliamentary election closes the playable campaign"
        : (Q.snap_campaign_active
        ? "The campaign ends with a constitutionally scheduled snap election still underway"
        : "The 2027 horizon closes after an earlier election reset the term");
}
!}

@final_assessment
